  "term": "voluntary retrieval",
  "definition": "Voluntary retrieval is the intentional recall of a memory through goal-directed memory search. In this source, it is described as reactivating temporally compressed, item-specific memory representations rather than the sensory-feature-based patterns seen in involuntary retrieval.",
